    },
    {
      type: 'cards', id: 'triggers', title: 'The Details That Can Change the Approval Path', nav: 'Approval Triggers',
      items: [
        { title: 'Size & height', text: 'Some jurisdictions treat accessory buildings differently once they pass a certain footprint, height or distance from property lines.' },
        { title: 'Use', text: 'Storage raises fewer questions than a building with power, heat, cooling, plumbing, a finished interior or daily use.' },
        { title: 'Location', text: 'Rear- and side-yard setbacks, drainage and utility easements, access limits and street visibility can affect placement.' },
        { title: 'Utilities', text: 'Electrical, HVAC and plumbing may bring trade permits, inspections, licensed work and trenching.' },
        { title: 'Foundation', text: 'Slab, pier, anchored or permanent-foundation conditions may be reviewed differently.' },
        { title: 'Appearance', text: 'Siding, color, roof, windows, screening and visibility can matter in HOA communities.' },
      ],
    },
    {
